# The Olympians

Kronos and Rhea had six children: Hestia, Demeter, Hera, Hades, Poseidon
and Zeus. Kronos swallowed each one at birth, except Zeus, whom Rhea hid in
Crete. The twelve gods of the Parthenon's east frieze are five of these
with seven of the next generation. Hades lives below, and Dionysus takes
the place among the twelve that Hestia sometimes has.

```hql id=gods hidden
import myth.kb
import myth.beings

kb.beings() | filter(b => b.olympian() or b.id == "hestia" or b.id == "hades")
```

## Names

Each Greek name as written, in Latin letters and without its marks, the
Roman name, and the god's article in [[wikipedia]]. The Latin letters and
the unmarked Greek come from the `greek` package, whose functions are
declared in HQL with no body and implemented in Rust. The articles come
from the table in the Wikipedia card, read through `@[[wikipedia]]`.

```hql
import myth.beings
import myth.wikipedia

articles = wikipedia.articles(@[[wikipedia]].body.unwrap_or(""))

gods
| map(b => {
    god: b.name,
    greek: b.greek,
    latin: b.latin(),
    unmarked: b.plain(),
    roman: b.roman.unwrap_or(""),
    wikipedia: wikipedia.article(articles, b.id) | map(a => a.link()) | unwrap_or(""),
  })
| Table(columns = ["god", "greek", "latin", "unmarked", "roman", "wikipedia"])
```
