## Family and domains

The parents each god has in the first account the knowledge base holds,
Hesiod's where Hesiod gives one. Where the sources disagree, as they do on
Aphrodite and Hephaestus, [[theogony]] sets the accounts side by side.

```hql
import myth.kb
import myth.beings
from myth.genealogy import parents_of

births = kb.parentage()

gods
| map(b => {god: b.name, parents: parents_of(births, b.id) | map(kb.name) | join(" and "), domains: b.domains | join(", ")})
| Table(columns = ["god", "parents", "domains"])
```
<!-- hql:output hash=77b84509647b status=ok -->
| god        | parents         | domains                                         |
| ---------- | --------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| Hestia     | Kronos and Rhea | hearth                                          |
| Demeter    | Kronos and Rhea | grain, agriculture, the Mysteries               |
| Hera       | Kronos and Rhea | marriage, queen of the gods                     |
| Hades      | Kronos and Rhea | the underworld, the dead                        |
| Poseidon   | Kronos and Rhea | sea, earthquakes, horses                        |
| Zeus       | Kronos and Rhea | sky, thunder, kingship, hospitality             |
| Athena     | Zeus and Metis  | wisdom, crafts, war strategy                    |
| Apollo     | Zeus and Leto   | prophecy, music, healing, the bow               |
| Artemis    | Zeus and Leto   | the hunt, wild animals, childbirth              |
| Ares       | Zeus and Hera   | war                                             |
| Aphrodite  | Uranus          | love, beauty, desire                            |
| Hephaestus | Hera            | fire, metalwork, the forge                      |
| Hermes     | Zeus and Maia   | messengers, travellers, thieves, guide of souls |
| Dionysus   | Zeus and Semele | wine, ecstasy, theatre                          |
<!-- /hql:output -->

## The children of Zeus

Every child any account gives Zeus: gods, the Muses and the Horae, and the
mortal-born Dionysus, Perseus and Heracles.

```hql
import myth.kb
import myth.beings
from myth.genealogy import children_of

children_of(kb.parentage(), "zeus")
| map(id => kb.being(id))
| somes
| map(b => {child: b.name, kind: b.kind})
| Table(columns = ["child", "kind"])
```
<!-- hql:output hash=cb8a6d1df60e status=ok -->
| child      | kind     |
| ---------- | -------- |
| Athena     | olympian |
| Horae      | deity    |
| Moirai     | deity    |
| Charites   | deity    |
| Persephone | deity    |
| Muses      | deity    |
| Apollo     | olympian |
| Artemis    | olympian |
| Hebe       | deity    |
| Ares       | olympian |
| Eileithyia | deity    |
| Hermes     | olympian |
| Dionysus   | olympian |
| Heracles   | hero     |
| Hephaestus | olympian |
| Aphrodite  | olympian |
| Perseus    | hero     |
<!-- /hql:output -->

## Their myths

How many of the myths in the knowledge base each god takes part in, and
the first of them in the order the myths happen.

```hql
import myth.kb
import myth.beings
import myth.stories

type Told { god : String, myths : Int, first : String }

told = kb.myths()

gods
| map(b => Told(
    god   = b.name,
    myths = told | filter(m => m.features(b.id)) | size,
    first = told | filter(m => m.features(b.id)) | first | map(m => m.title) | unwrap_or(""),
  ))
| sort(by = r => 0 - r.myths)
| Table(columns = ["god", "myths", "first"])
```
<!-- hql:output hash=56056159df4d status=ok -->
| god        | myths | first                                  |
| ---------- | ----- | -------------------------------------- |
| Zeus       | 21    | Kronos swallows his children           |
| Hera       | 9     | Kronos swallows his children           |
| Athena     | 9     | The war of the Giants                  |
| Hephaestus | 5     | Pandora                                |
| Hades      | 4     | Kronos swallows his children           |
| Poseidon   | 4     | Kronos swallows his children           |
| Apollo     | 4     | The birth of Apollo and Artemis        |
| Hermes     | 4     | Hermes steals the cattle of Apollo     |
| Demeter    | 2     | Kronos swallows his children           |
| Artemis    | 2     | The birth of Apollo and Artemis        |
| Ares       | 2     | Ares and Aphrodite in Hephaestus's net |
| Aphrodite  | 2     | Kronos castrates Uranus                |
| Dionysus   | 2     | The birth of Dionysus                  |
| Hestia     | 1     | Kronos swallows his children           |
<!-- /hql:output -->
